==Battleground==
*4 [[Pigge Back]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~33.33 seconds<sup>500f~1,000f</sup>.
**4 [[Pigge Back]]s spawn, delay 33.33~50 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,500f</sup>.
**2 [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
**2 [[Dead Donny Dash|Dead Donny Dashes]] spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since this stage drops [[Lucky Capsule|Lucky Ticket G]], it's advised to use a strategy which can be repeated consistently and quickly in order to farm them efficiently.

Rushing this stage is simple with a [[Double Bounty]] unit, [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], and another [[Rusher class Cats|rusher]] to supplement him (such as [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]]). Bring along Attack Up [[Cat Combo|Cat Combos]] as well, since this strategy and its variants depend heavily on being able to kill Lord Gravey quickly so he can deal as little damage as possible.

Begin by killing the first Pigge Back with a Double Bounty unit. This can be done by crippling said walking piggy bank with a [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] into reaping its reward with [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. Afterward, spawn Bahamut immediately to ensure he causes an [[Explosion]] on base impact. This lethal burst should immediately vaporize the wave of peons, providing a much-needed cash injection. Spawn the supplementary rusher to quickly kill Lord Gravey, as even a fully-talented Lv50 Bahamut with two Attack Up (Sm) Cat Combos can't solo it in time.

Assuming everything is done correctly, the sheer amount of damage toward Lord Gravey will kill him, leaving the base wide open for a brief deadly assault. If Lord Gravey is killing Bahamut or [[Revive|reviving]] before the base is destroyed, the supplementary rusher isn't putting in enough work and should be replaced or further supported.

=== Recommended Units ===

* [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Provides a slightly faster way of farming the opening peon. At Lv50+8 with a fully maxed Attack Buff Talent and two Attack Up (Sm) Cat Combos, they're just barely able to OHKO the Pigge Back.
* [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Can be used as a supplementary rusher, since their [[Long Distance]] allows them to chip the enemy base.
* Awakened Bahamut Cat: The crux of all rushdown strategies, as explained above.
* Idi:N: Helps clean up Lord Gravey and the base by giving your frontlines the boost it needs.

=== Recommended Ubers ===

* [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: A supplementary rusher with extremely high movement speed, ensuring he deals damage soon after being deployed.
* [[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Vampiric Yukimura]]: Within the same niche as his non-seasonal counterpart. Despite his unique [[Survive]], neither he nor his progenitor should be dying to Lord Gravey at Lv30.
* [[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Bloody Jack]]: With an incredible 18k DPS and 119k HP at just Lv30, spawning him after Bahamut can clean up a botched strategy, since he'll destroy the base even if Lord Gravey revives. He also functions as a sole supplementary rusher with his [[Knockback]], continuously interrupting Lord Gravey's attack or by letting Bahamut sneak a hit into the enemy base.

